ios: minimap zoom

For the mobile HUD's minimap zoom slider: setMinimapZoom(zoom) draws the minimap at `zoom` times its pixels per tile,
0.5..2 (1 = upstream, 4 px per tile). The anti-macro wobble (macroMinimapZoom) stays on top. The map, the dots, the
hint arrow and a tap on the map (minimapLoop) all use the zoomed scale, and the dots' range and the arrow's switch to a
plain dot are measured on the map. hudState() reports minimapZoom. Zoomed out, the map can reach past the black margin
of the minimap image (the player can stand 16 tiles from its edge), so it is drawn clipped (Pix32
scanlineRotatePlotSpriteClipped: black there, where upstream's sampling wraps round to the other side); below 2/3 it
samples a half-size copy of the image (Pix32.halved, the mean of each 2x2, made once per map build), as every other
pixel would skip the map's 1 px walls. Unzoomed, nothing changes.

